# AF-EP-003 — Enterprise Information Flow

**Project:** BTA V5.1 — HCGO Enterprise Persistence Architecture

**Status:** Approved

**Classification:** Analysis Finding

---

# Purpose

Identify the authorized flow of enterprise information across HCGO.

This analysis establishes authorized enterprise information flow prior to Enterprise Conceptual Information Modeling and Persistence Architecture.

This analysis identifies enterprise information flow only.

It does not define runtime execution, orchestration, APIs, persistence, messaging, implementation, or technology.

---

# Analysis Principles

Enterprise Information Flow shall identify:

- Enterprise Information Categories
- Authoritative ownership
- Information providers
- Authorized consumers
- Authorized references
- Enterprise relationships
- Information dependencies
- Authorized information exchanges

Enterprise Information Flow shall not identify:

- Runtime execution
- Service invocation
- APIs
- Messaging
- Database tables
- Foreign keys
- PostgreSQL schema
- Persistence implementation
- Technology implementation

---

# Enterprise Information Flow Principles

Every Enterprise Information Category shall originate from one and only one authoritative enterprise owner, who inherently serves as the authoritative provider of that information.

Enterprise information may flow only to authorized consumers or authorized reference capabilities.

Information flow never transfers ownership.

Consumers may consume information.

Reference capabilities may observe, classify, validate, or audit information without becoming consumers.

Enterprise information flow defines enterprise authorization relationships only.

It does not define runtime execution, orchestration, APIs, persistence, messaging, or implementation.

